# If a module that only an `import()` names counted as one that is in the program for the host's sake, it would be evaluated and all that it exports would escape, though no run comes to the `import()`
# main.js: enum Mode { On = 1 }  if (Mode.On !== 1) (await import("./behind.js")).dead();  function never() { return import("./other.js") }
# behind.js: export function dead() {}    other.js: export function alsoDead() {}
# `import()` stands in no list of requests. The operation names the module: in a block that constants rule out (m1), and in a function that nothing reaches (m2).
# RUN: summary f0 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: names-where-no-run-comes m1
# CHECK: never-entered b1
# RUN(LINK): link functions mechanisms=all
# LINK: function f0
# LINK-NOT: unreached
# LINK: function f1 unreached
# LINK: function f2 unreached
# LINK: function f3 unreached
# LINK: function f4 unreached
# LINK: function f5 unreached
# With Folding withheld the walk builds the `import()`, so the scan has looked at it. What only `never` names stays out.
# RUN(BOTH): link functions mechanisms=-Folding
# BOTH-NOT: function f1 unreached
# BOTH-NOT: function f2 unreached
# BOTH: function f3 unreached
# BOTH: function f4 unreached
# BOTH: function f5 unreached
# RUN(UNITS): units-with-code f1:Body f2:Body f4:Body f5:Body mechanisms=all
# UNITS: unit f1:Body has no code
# UNITS: unit f2:Body has no code
# UNITS: unit f4:Body has no code
# UNITS: unit f5:Body has no code
# RUN(ALL): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ALL: exited with 0
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=none
# NONE: exited with 0

